  "action_summary": "Round 25 went one layer below inference, to PERCEPTION, and found something the pre-registration did not predict. P1 was confirmed: derive_probe_space raised TypeError on any list/dict/set input, so four rounds of inference work had never been shown a container. Fixed with canonical_key(). P2 was confirmed: every probe was tuple([x]*arity), so a two-argument task was only ever observed at f(n,n); non-diagonal probes were added and x*y then solved. The pre-registration then FALSIFIED ITSELF on the reason x*y+1 still refused: the grammar was never the limit. ((x0*x1)+1) is found in 64 ms at the synthesizer's own default bank of 900, but every organ-graph call site searched with max_bank_size 64-80, and at 72 the bank fills (72/72) and misses it. The organ graph reported NO_CONSISTENT_HYPOTHESIS -- a statement about the language -- for a limit that was a statement about an integer, while evidence_demand_v1 already had SEARCH_TRUNCATED for exactly this case. Coverage is now recorded on every miss, four call sites escalate a 72/900/5000 ladder only while the failure is a budget, a truncated search now reports SEARCH_TRUNCATED, and one collecting sweep decides grammar-exhausted vs budget-exhausted so the refusal names its real cause. Widening the search exposed three further pre-existing defects: a memorising STUN body crystallised as a law for x*y-7 (16 where the truth is 193), now rejected structurally by _is_a_restatement because it branches on EQUALITY with an observed input rather than an inequality; a one-slot probe tuple in two places in _grow_operator_from_evidence that crashed the oracle for every multi-argument task; and a zero-degree-of-freedom affine fit (x*x+y over three points) that is recorded as xfail(strict) for the next round rather than hidden. P4 (the 4x table-evidence constant) was measured and left open, recorded rather than rushed.",
